{
  "abstract": "Exclusive photoproduction cross sections have been measured for the processes \u03b3p\u2192\u03c0+n, \u03b3p\u2192\u03c00p, \u03b3p\u2192\u03c0\u2212\u0394++, \u03b3p\u2192\u03c10p, \u03b3p\u2192K+\u039b, and \u03b3p\u2192K+\u03a30 at large t and u values at several energies for each process between 4 and 7.5 GeV. These measurements taken together with past data taken at small values of t and u provide complete angular distributions. The data show the usual small t and u peaks and a central region in which the cross section decreases approximately as s\u22127. The results are discussed within the context of parton or constituent models.",
